#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:330
#: 87eed13fb55c4573be593d6e42075361
msgid "TKOFF\\_THR\\_IDLE: Takeoff idle throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:333
#: e639592348094eb2818892ed8f804255
msgid "The idle throttle to hold after arming and before a takeoff\\. Applicable in TAKEOFF and AUTO modes\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:348
#: 76bb0d76cda743fcb9f57cf6606c2ba1
msgid "TKOFF\\_OPTIONS: Takeoff options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:352
#: bf70a46dd890477e9458c901948201f2
msgid "This selects the mode of the takeoff in AUTO and TAKEOFF flight modes\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:361
#: 6173e85dda814cfba4ae005567b9cd75
msgid "When unset the maximum allowed throttle is always used (THR_MAX or TKOFF_THR_MAX) during takeoff. When set TECS is allowed to operate between a minimum (THR_MIN or TKOFF_THR_MIN) and a maximum (THR_MAX or TKOFF_THR_MAX) limit. Applicable only when using an airspeed sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:372
#: f1d88b8c63de42e0bdc19b4f42de872c
msgid "TKOFF\\_TDRAG\\_ELEV: Takeoff tail dragger elevator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:375
#: 6ef7cddc17aa44759be266984b812676
msgid "This parameter sets the amount of elevator to apply during the initial stage of a takeoff\\. It is used to hold the tail wheel of a taildragger on the ground during the initial takeoff stage to give maximum steering\\. This option should be combined with the TKOFF\\_TDRAG\\_SPD1 option and the GROUND\\_STEER\\_ALT option along with tuning of the ground steering controller\\. A value of zero means to bypass the initial \\\"tail hold\\\" stage of takeoff\\. Set to zero for hand and catapult launch\\. For tail\\-draggers you should normally set this to 100\\, meaning full up elevator during the initial stage of takeoff\\. For most tricycle undercarriage aircraft a value of zero will work well\\, but for some tricycle aircraft a small negative value \\(say around \\-20 to \\-30\\) will apply down elevator which will hold the nose wheel firmly on the ground during initial acceleration\\. Only use a negative value if you find that the nosewheel doesn\\'t grip well during takeoff\\. Too much down elevator on a tricycle undercarriage may cause instability in steering as the plane pivots around the nosewheel\\. Add down elevator 10 percent at a time\\."
msgstr ""

