#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1919
#: bcb66e6468d2442eab6691cab80f712d
msgid "MIXING\\_GAIN: Mixing Gain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1922
#: 48e0ab338d034bc6a417ff0e4332661f
msgid "The gain for the Vtail and elevon output mixers\\. The default is 0\\.5\\, which ensures that the mixer doesn\\'t saturate\\, allowing both input channels to go to extremes while retaining control over the output\\. Hardware mixers often have a 1\\.0 gain\\, which gives more servo throw\\, but can saturate\\. If you don\\'t have enough throw on your servos with VTAIL\\_OUTPUT or ELEVON\\_OUTPUT enabled then you can raise the gain using MIXING\\_GAIN\\. The mixer allows outputs in the range 900 to 2100 microseconds\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1928
#: d46eea925e514ef9908c1d6770870eaf
msgid "0.5 to 1.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1937
#: f8901697fcf34c86b80859f65f36a9ec
msgid "RUDDER\\_ONLY: Rudder only aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1940
#: fe336e62ead34f5f82f3dcd289287b73
msgid "Enable rudder only mode\\. The rudder will control attitude in attitude controlled modes \\(such as FBWA\\)\\. You should setup your transmitter to send roll stick inputs to the RCMAP\\_YAW channel \\(normally channel 4\\)\\. The rudder servo should be attached to the RCMAP\\_YAW channel as well\\. Note that automatic ground steering will be disabled for rudder only aircraft\\. You should also set KFF\\_RDDRMIX to 1\\.0\\. You will also need to setup the YAW2SRV\\_DAMP yaw damping appropriately for your aircraft\\. A value of 0\\.5 for YAW2SRV\\_DAMP is a good starting point\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1962
#: e269e69411c1471aaea47fc43b0b9700
msgid "MIXING\\_OFFSET: Mixing Offset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:1965
#: cfebf71f8733494caabfd9e31b65a142
msgid "The offset for the Vtail and elevon output mixers\\, as a percentage\\. This can be used in combination with MIXING\\_GAIN to configure how the control surfaces respond to input\\. The response to aileron or elevator input can be increased by setting this parameter to a positive or negative value\\. A common usage is to enter a positive value to increase the aileron response of the elevons of a flying wing\\. The default value of zero will leave the aileron\\-input response equal to the elevator\\-input response\\."
msgstr ""

