msgid "FWD\\_BAT\\_THR\\_CUT: Forward throttle cutoff battery voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:2930
#: 377fbd0fe5aa424dbd5520fc16b0f892
msgid "The estimated battery resting voltage below which the throttle is cut in auto\\-throttle modes\\. Measured on the battery used for forward throttle compensation \\(FWD\\_BAT\\_IDX\\)\\. If set to zero\\, the throttle will not be cut due to low voltage\\, allowing the motor\\(s\\) to continue running until the battery is depleted\\. This should be set to the minimum operating voltage of you motor\\(s\\) or to a voltage level where minimal thrust is produced\\, to conserve the remaining battery power for the electronics and actuators\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:2936
#: be8094ab9031409cbf78c8e566aab1f6
msgid "0 to 35"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:2945
#: 18031c031d984a0f98e9a8aaeb72bdee
msgid "CLIMB\\_SLOPE\\_HGT: Climb slope minimum height"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:2949
#: 08948543959c4d9cb42cd31df3fc0ac4
msgid "Sets the minimum height above home at which the aircraft will apply a climb slope between waypoints\\. Below it\\, the aircraft will ascend immediately\\, and will only resume the requested trajectory upon reaching this height\\. This prevents unsafe behavior such as attempting to slowly gain altitude near obstacles\\. The default value ensures safe operations in most environments\\, but it can be adjusted based on specific terrain or operational needs\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:2964
#: 6784fb21714c4e6a8aa0df2aedae193d
msgid "GUIDED\\_TIMEOUT: Timeout for external guided command\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:2968
#: f158645f5a194e7cbf73f72e11971dc1
msgid "If external guided command was not received by this timeout\\, the vehicle will revert to regular GUIDED mode\\."
msgstr ""

